instruction:
Create API interfaces for the following endpoints with corresponding DTOs and OpenAPI schemas:

Authentication:
- POST /auth/register: Request {email: string, password: string} → Response {token: string, user: {id: number, email: string, role: 'user' | 'admin' | 'super-admin'}}
- POST /auth/login: Request {email: string, password: string} → Response {token: string, user: ...}
- PUT /auth/me/password: Request {currentPassword: string, newPassword: string}
- DELETE /auth/me: Delete user account (includes cascade deletion of articles/comments)

User Profile:
- GET /users/me: Get current user profile (auth required)
- PUT /users/me: Update profile {displayName: string, bio: string}
- GET /users/{id}: Get public profile (id: number)

Sections:
- GET /sections: List all sections (public)
- POST /sections: Create section (admin required) {name: string, description: string}
- PUT /sections/{id}: Update section (admin)
- DELETE /sections/{id}: Delete section (admin)

Articles:
- GET /articles: List articles (public) [query: page=1, limit=20, sort='newest' | 'oldest', search='text', tags='tag1,tag2']
- POST /articles: Create article (auth required) {title: string, content: string, sectionId: number, files: File[], images: File[], tags: string[]}
- GET /articles/{id}: Get single article (public) - includes full content, attachments, tags
- PUT /articles/{id}: Update article (owner/admin) {title, content, files, images, tags}
- DELETE /articles/{id}: Delete article (owner/admin)

Comments:
- GET /articles/{id}/comments: List comments (public) (sort: oldest first)
- POST /articles/{id}/comments: Create comment {content: string}
- PUT /comments/{id}: Update comment (owner) {content}
- DELETE /comments/{id}: Delete comment (owner)

Admin:
- POST /admin/request: Submit request {reason: string} (auth: user)
- GET /admin/requests: List pending requests (auth: super-admin)
- PUT /admin/requests/{id}: Update request {status: 'approved' | 'rejected'}
- POST /admin/upgrade: Upgrade to super-admin (auth: super-admin) {userId}
- POST /admin/downgrade: Downgrade (auth: super-admin) {userId}
- POST /bans: Ban user (auth: super-admin) {userId, reason}
- DELETE /bans/{userId}: Unban user (auth: super-admin)
- GET /bans: List banned users (auth: admin)

All endpoints require authentication via Bearer token. File attachments use multipart/form-data. SectionId must be valid. All POST/PUT require validation of required fields.

